# Build-context exclusions for `docker build` / `docker compose build`.
#
# Two separate problems this solves, both found during the 2026-08-16
# pre-deployment pass (F-006):
#
# 1. Context size. Without this file the context was ~370MB, almost all of
#    it frontend/node_modules, data/ and .git -- none of which any COPY in
#    the Dockerfile ever references.
#
# 2. Correctness, which matters more. The frontend-build stage runs
#    `npm ci` and THEN `COPY frontend/ ./`, so the host's own
#    frontend/node_modules was copied straight over the image's freshly
#    installed one. That happened to work here only because this host and
#    the node:20-slim base image are both linux/x64 on Node 20 -- a macOS
#    or ARM developer would have silently shipped native binaries built
#    for the wrong platform into the image. Excluding node_modules from
#    the context means that COPY can no longer clobber anything, and the
#    `npm ci` layer finally gets to earn its build cache.

.git
.gitignore
data
node_modules
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
tests/e2e/ui/node_modules
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
docs/e2e-artifacts
